        "math_academy_id": "q-10564",
        "problem": "Calculate $\\int (2-\\frac{x}{2}+2{cot}^{2}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        "worked_solution": "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}\u2061x={csc}^{2}\u2061x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cot}^{2}\u2061x & ={csc}^{2}\u2061x-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2-\\frac{x}{2}+2{cot}^{2}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2-\\frac{x}{2}+2({csc}^{2}\u2061x-1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2-\\frac{x}{2}+2{csc}^{2}\u2061x-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (-\\frac{x}{2}+2{csc}^{2}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-2\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
